hi guys it's me quinn and as always if  you appreciate my content consider  hitting the like button it's the only  way the youtube algorithm really notices  me  six singles remembrance verse past  series has become one of my top science  fiction series since i read it last year  keep in mind this video will have some  spoilers for the series  there are many haunting philosophical  quandaries brought up by the three body  problem series  but there is one that stuck with me more  than the others  one of the themes that weaves its way  throughout all of six and those books  revolves around whether or not we can  actually trust that our understanding of  the universe actually reflects its true  nature  as far as we can tell the universe is  about 14 billion years old  we calculate this by finding the oldest  stars and by measuring the rate of  expansion of the universe  by observing the current state of the  universe we can calculate backwards  towards the big bang  according to our best estimates there  are around 2 trillion galaxies in the  universe  200 billion trillion stars  and over 700 quintillion planets the  universe is estimated to be 28 billion  parsecs across  it would take light the fastest moving  thing in the universe 93 billion years  to go from one side to the other  hearing these numbers you might assume  that we understand a lot about the  universe  but in actuality all of these estimates  are barely more than educated guesses  the two things that seem clearest are  that the universe is incredibly old and  incredibly big it would be extremely  arrogant of us to think that from our  vantage point here on a tiny blue ball  orbiting a medium-sized star in a nine  planet solar system somewhere in a  lonely dark corner of the cosmos we  could actually grasp a full  understanding of the intricate  mechanisms that form the universe  we can only approximate  scientists accept that much of our  knowledge of the cosmos is subject to  change as we learn more about its nature  as research unveils never before  realized secrets of the universe and as  technologies make it easier for us to  observe our surroundings our  understanding of the cosmos evolves  the suggestion made in the three-body  problem series is however more  devastating than the idea of science  gradually being updated based on  advances in knowledge and technology  what if we are not merely wrong about a  few things  what if our entire understanding of what  the universe is and how it works is  wrong  the universe does in fact seem ancient  if it is at least 14 billion years old  as our science suggests  then probability would suggest that  there should have been countless  civilizations to exist before mankind  as i discussed in my last three-body  problem video the drake equation  suggests that the universe should be  full of other life  and if this is true then what potential  effect has said life had on the universe  considering the immense effect that the  existence of life has had upon the earth  in the third book in the series death  sinned the character yang yandong  witnesses a simulation depicting earth  throughout time with the variable of  life removed  in the modern era earth was a twin of  mars  humans often underestimated the effect  that life has had on the environment of  earth when yangdong considers this  concept and applies it to the universe  which she at this point in the story  understood was full of alien beings her  mind is brought to a new chilling  concept  if what we see when we look into the  cosmos is the universe exploding with  life  then what would it look like without  life  she tried to stop thinking  to turn her mind into empty darkness  but a new question stubbornly refused to  leave her alone  is nature really natural  nature as we see it may not be in fact  natural at all  the three body problem provides two  analogies and an attempt to explain this  concept  one far darker than the other  there is the shooter hypothesis on the  farmer hypothesis  we will start with the shooter  hypothesis  in the shooter hypothesis a good  marksman shoots at a target creating a  hole every 10 centimeters  now suppose the surface of the target is  inhabited by intelligent two-dimensional  creatures  their scientists after observing the  universe discover a great law  there exist a hole in the universe every  10 centimeters they have mistaken the  result of the marksman's momentary whim  for an unalterable law of the universe  we are observing the universe from a  particular place and time a blip on the  cosmic scale  just because the universe appears to us  in a certain way now does not mean that  it has always been this way or that it  will always be we are in this analogy  the two-dimensional beings only able to  measure the state of the universe as it  exists from our perspective  the universe may be operating based on  intricate schematics beyond our ability  to comprehend  to further drive home this point is the  farmer hypothesis  the far darker of the two analogies  every morning on a turkey farm the  farmer comes to feed the turkeys  a scientist turkey having observed this  pattern to hold without change for  almost a year  makes the following discovery  every morning at 11 food arrives  on the morning of thanksgiving the  scientist announces this law to the  other turkeys but that morning at 11 the  food doesn't arrive instead the farmer  comes and kills the entire flock  what is the universe  what is its nature to think that we can  know beyond a shadow of a doubt is to be  as arrogant as the scientist turkey  we must consider that the universe may  have a deadly and eldritch function  one that if we could fully comprehend  might cause us to cry out in existential  agony  this hypothesis can also be viewed as  placing an emphasis on the potential  life that formed in the darkness of the  universe before we did  a high enough level civilization would  have almost god-like potential compared  to us in this metaphor they would be the  farmer and we the turkeys our place in  the universe could be a comfortable  illusion  for all we know we could already be in  the belly of the beast  this idea manifest itself in the series  in two clear ways  the alien beings known as the  tricelerins creation of sofons which  invisibly stifled the progress of human  development by rendering physics  unreliable from within our region of  space  and the existence of eons of  interactions and wars between the higher  dimensional beings that once inhabited  the higher dimensional universe before  it was gradually degraded by life we  discussed the latter in my video the  mystery of the fourth dimension the  trisolarene sophons are the most direct  example  the sophons operate it based on quantum  mechanical principles the word quantum  refers to the minimum unit of any  physical entity involved in interaction  so sophons were in fact very small  though they could unfold into higher  dimensions  sophons were essentially supercomputers  etched onto a proton  because of the principles of quantum  entanglement sophons on earth provided a  stream of instantaneous information  about earth to the tricelerin home world  in real time they watched and studied  the human race  the sofon supercomputer could impede the  progress of scientific development  wherever necessary and humankind was  incapable of stopping it they had  already been crippled  our understanding of the universe would  ultimately hit a standstill  the tricelerians would not allow any  development that could prevent their  invasion and habitation of the earth  in the first book in the series we  learned that scientists in different  fields throughout the world had been  committing suicide yandong included  this turned out to be the reason why  upon discovering that their entire lives  spent studying their particular feelings  of science had been rendered useless  they could not cope  humankind does eventually begin to  develop ways to thwart the tricelerins  the tricelerins do not have access to  the thoughts hidden away within the  human mind and the aliens unlike human  beings do not fully grasp the concept of  deception  because of this humanity invents the  wall face of project which we will go  into more detail about in another video  the struggle between humanity and the  tricelerians continues for centuries  both sides suffer greatly in the end  humanity would eventually learn that  there were others far more powerful and  deadlier than the trisolarens  our interaction with the inhabitants of  the trisolera  had itself been a mere blip on the  cosmic timeline  thank you guys so much for watching make  sure you like and subscribe for more  science fiction videos
 

